---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CaseGallery from "../../../components/CaseGallery.astro";
import CaseNext from "../../../components/CaseNext.astro";
import ProjectMedia from "../../../components/ProjectMedia.astro";
import { caseStudies } from "../../../data/site";
import { caseStudyJsonLd } from "../../../utils/seo";

const study = caseStudies.find((item) => item.slug === "robinberzinmd")!;
---

<BaseLayout
  pilot
  title={`${study.name} publishing platform case study`}
  description={study.summary}
  path="/case-studies/robinberzinmd/"
  image={study.image}
  jsonLd={caseStudyJsonLd(study.slug)}
>
  <section class="case-hero" data-analytics-component="case_study">
    <p class="kicker">{study.label}</p>
    <h1>{study.name}</h1>
    <p>{study.summary}</p>
    <p class="case-context">Publishing platform · agentic content pipeline · collage art direction</p>
    <a class="text-link" href={study.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit live site</a>
  </section>
  <ProjectMedia study={study} class="case-image" eager />
  <section class="robin-art-intro" aria-labelledby="robin-art-title">
    <p class="kicker">Editorial visual system</p>
    <h2 id="robin-art-title">An illustration style built for the whole story.</h2>
    <p>AI-assisted cut-paper collage, shaped by editorial art direction, gives each topic one clear visual idea. Separate landscape and portrait compositions carry that language across the site, email, and social formats.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="robin-art-gallery">
    <CaseGallery title={`${study.shortName} collage illustrations`} items={study.gallery} />
  </div>
  <section class="case-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>{study.problem}</p>
      <h2 class="case-gap">Delivered capability</h2>
      <p class="case-result"><strong>{study.result.stat}</strong><span>{study.result.label}</span></p>
      <p>{study.outcome}</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Role and delivery</h2>
      <p>David led the product structure, site build, art direction, and publishing workflow. The work joined editorial organization, article production, and routes to subscription and inquiry.</p>
      <ul>
        {study.work.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <h2 class="case-gap">Product decisions</h2>
      <p>Organize the breadth of content so a new reader can find a useful starting point, then make the next step visible in context. Treat newsletter signup and inquiry as distinct journeys. Preserve Robin's authored prose while adapting each issue for the formats around it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="robin-pipeline" aria-labelledby="robin-pipeline-title">
    <div class="robin-pipeline-heading">
      <p class="kicker">How the publishing system works</p>
      <h2 id="robin-pipeline-title">One source, several useful outputs.</h2>
      <p>Agentic steps prepare and check the work; editors retain the final decision. The pipeline creates release-ready material for Robin's site, Off Script newsletter, and social channels without treating AI-generated copy as Robin's voice.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="robin-pipeline-steps">
      <li><span>01</span><h3>Start with Robin's draft</h3><p>A final Google Doc enters a Ready folder. The workflow preserves Robin's prose, headings, links, and authored protocol.</p></li>
      <li><span>02</span><h3>Build the web edition</h3><p>The workflow prepares the article page, topics, search details, citations, and reader paths. Editors review a preview before the site changes go live.</p></li>
      <li><span>03</span><h3>Make art for each format</h3><p>The system generates separate landscape and portrait cut-paper compositions, then prepares a feed card, captions, and tracked links for social distribution.</p></li>
      <li><span>04</span><h3>Review before release</h3><p>A native Beehiiv draft is formatted and tested. People approve the site release and newsletter send; the social package is handed off for channel posting.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <CaseNext currentSlug={study.slug} />
</BaseLayout>
